   "evidence": "This idea combines verified facts: low competition for Tinker, Temporal and Entire; Tinker can run without your own GPU; Temporal's starter code works through LiteLLM; Entire is easy to add; small models are weak at strict JSON. The idea itself is untested. Fallbacks: if Tinker credits or cost turn out to be a blocker, aim for DigitalOcean instead (featured, about 1 mention) by serving the open model on a GPU Droplet or the Gradient AI Platform. Choose Arduino (0 mentions) only if you already own an UNO Q board.",
