 "caveats": "The saturation counts are a snapshot from 2026-10-10 of a feed growing by roughly 150-200 posts a day. A last-day surge before the Oct 11, 11:59 PM PDT deadline could change the ranking. The counts match sponsor names in titles, descriptions and tags only, not the Prize Categories sections inside post bodies, so they stand in for real entries and probably undercount them. Using a sponsor's technology, especially Gemma, is not the same as entering its category. The hot-topics part of the research question (fall foliage, BirdCast and eBird migration, frost dates, smoke, trail conditions) produced NO verified claims, and the data sources named in the recommended idea (weather, migration forecasts) were not checked. Tinker pricing and free credits are unverified; the $150 promotional credit figure comes from a third party. The DigitalOcean and Arduino build paths were not researched. Swapping Temporal's starter code to a local open model is inferred from LiteLLM support and has not been demonstrated. Last year's winners show every category draws at least one entry, so 'nobody will build on it' is not literally true. The recommended idea is a synthesis and has not been built or tested.",
